      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "We start with the given information that when \\( n \\) is divided by 6, the remainder is 1. This can be expressed mathematically as:\n\\[\nn \\equiv 1 \\pmod{6}\n\\]\nWe need to find the remainder when \\( n + 2010 \\) is divided by 6. To do this, we first express \\( n + 2010 \\) in terms of the congruence relation:\n\\[\nn + 2010 \\equiv 1 + 2010 \\pmod{6}\n\\]\nNext, we simplify \\( 2010 \\) modulo 6:\n\\[\n2010 \\div 6 = 335 \\text{ with no remainder}\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\n2010 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{6}\n\\]\nSubstituting this back into our congruence, we get:\n\\[\nn + 2010 \\equiv 1 + 0 \\pmod{6}\n\\]\n\\[\nn + 2010 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{6}\n\\]\nTherefore, the remainder when \\( n + 2010 \\) is divided by 6 is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]",
